Subject: [Pico Linux] Backport stable DRM timeline sync objects

Import drm_syncobj.c/h from Linux v5.4.302 (9e3157c56ec7), with the
matching timeline UAPI, ioctl registration and binary caller adaptation.
Keep the vendor feature mask layout: 0x80000 is already XBGR_30BPP, so
assign the new internal timeline capability the unused 0x100000 bit.
Enable it on SDE only with the core implementation present. KGSL submission
continues through the existing sync_file bridge, not an MSM GPU driver.
Upstream authors and licenses are retained. See docs/pico-drm-timeline-backport.md.

